 7. 🩻 Charted: America&#x27;s ER waits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services. Map: Jim Sergent/Axios Americans now spend an average of more than 2.5 hours in hospital emergency departments, Axios' Maya Goldman reports from new federal data .

 ⏲️ The average time spent in the emergency department was 162 minutes.

 D.C . had the highest average visit length — 303 minutes. North Dakota had the lowest, with 110 minutes. ‼️ An average of 2% of patients nationwide left the ER before being seen.

