 8. 📺 1 trend to go: Nostalgic teen TV 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The cast of "Sterling Point" in Times Square. Photo: Jason Mendez/Getty Images for Prime Video Adults are finding a nostalgic summer escape in teen shows that evoke the good old days.

 The latest: Amazon Prime Video renewed "Sterling Point" for a second season after it held the streamer's top spot for most of the month.

 It's Amazon's third coming-of-age renewal this year, along with "Off Campus" and "Every Year After," Deadline notes . 🇨🇦 The sun-drenched series on Canada's rural Lake Muskoka is part of a wave of teen shows that stash the phones and reference a more lo-fi past, The Guardian's Emma Madden observes :

 "At a moment defined by social media loneliness and atomization, they place love, sex and intimacy back within reach, creating analog worlds built around face-to-face connection." 
 
